From: efx <volvox@stalya.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-efx: identify cards at 400 kHz

The driver reported a quarter of the base clock as its lowest frequency, so
the core identified cards at 25 MHz instead of 400 kHz. SD cards put up with
it, but an eMMC answers CMD1 on an open-drain CMD line that its pull-up
cannot raise that fast, and never initialises. Report the base clock through
the largest divider the driver uses, 390 kHz from 100 MHz.

---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-efx.c	2026-09-23 15:07:22.313568038 +0300
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-efx.c	2026-09-23 15:07:22.319785881 +0300
@@ -198,14 +198,17 @@
 	return pltfm_host->clock;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The lowest clock is the base clock through the largest divider
+ * efx_sdhci_set_clock() picks (SDHCI_MAX_DIV_SPEC_200). The core identifies
+ * a card at max(400 kHz, f_min), and an eMMC answers CMD1 on an open-drain
+ * CMD line, which its pull-up cannot raise at a quarter of the base clock.
+ */
 static unsigned int efx_sdhci_get_min_clock(struct sdhci_host *host)
 {
-	unsigned int f_min;
 	struct sdhci_pltfm_host *pltfm_host = sdhci_priv(host);
 
-	f_min = pltfm_host->clock / 4;
-
-	return f_min;
+	return pltfm_host->clock / SDHCI_MAX_DIV_SPEC_200;
 }
 
 static int efx_sdhci_get_cd(struct mmc_host *host)
